1. a raise inside rescue sets cause automatically
   High: "save failed"; cause: Low: "disk full"
2. cause: sets it explicitly, to any exception object
   e.cause.class Low; the same object: true
3. cause: nil hides the exception being handled
   e.cause nil
4. a chain of three, walked with cause
   [High, Mid, Low]
5. what full_message prints about the chain (labels only)
   '<main>': h (High)
   '<main>': m (Mid)
   '<main>': l (Low)
6. no rescue in progress: cause is nil
   e.cause nil
7. a cause chain may not loop
   raise a, cause: b while b's cause is a -> ArgumentError: "circular causes"
8. a raise inside ensure, while another exception is in flight, gets a cause too
   inner.cause.class Low
   the body's Low still reaches the outer rescue
9. cause is read-only
   Exception.method_defined?(:cause=) false
